📘 Prompt Document: Guardrail Scaffolding Specification

For an Agent that Generates All Files, Folders, Scripts, and Components

🎯 Objective

Generate a complete, reproducible, multi‑layer guardrail system that enforces the invariant:

automations.yaml must always contain a valid YAML list ([]).

This guardrail must be enforced across:

GitHub (CI)

Home Assistant (pre‑flight add‑on)

Local development (VS Code tasks)

Cluster automation (Ansible role)

XPipe command packs

Documentation (Mermaid diagrams + folder structure)

The agent must scaffold all files, folders, scripts, and configuration needed to implement this system.

📂 1. Required Folder Structure

The agent must generate the following directory tree:

repo-root/
├── home-assistant/
│   ├── automations.yaml
│   ├── python_scripts/
│   │   └── ensure_automation_list.py
│   ├── guardrails/
│   │   ├── validate_automations.py
│   │   ├── schema.yaml
│   │   └── README.md
│
├── tools/
│   ├── xpipe/
│   │   └── guardrail-pack.json
│   ├── vscode/
│   │   └── tasks.json
│   └── hooks/
│       └── pre-commit
│
├── ansible/
│   └── roles/
│       └── ha_guardrail/
│           ├── tasks/main.yml
│           └── defaults/main.yml
│
├── github/
│   └── workflows/
│       └── guardrail.yml
│
├── addons/
│   └── ha-preflight-guardrail/
│       ├── config.yaml
│       ├── Dockerfile
│       └── guardrail.sh
│
├── docs/
│   ├── ha-copilot/
│   │   ├── guardrails.md
│   │   └── troubleshooting.md
│   └── diagrams/
│       └── guardrail-flow.mmd
│
└── README.md

🧩 2. Required Files and Their Contents

The agent must generate the following files with full content:

2.1 Home Assistant Guardrail Scripts

automations.yaml containing []

python_scripts/ensure_automation_list.py

guardrails/validate_automations.py

guardrails/schema.yaml

guardrails/README.md

2.2 GitHub Action

.github/workflows/guardrail.ymlValidates automations.yaml on every push/PR.

2.3 Pre‑flight HA Supervisor Add-on

addons/ha-preflight-guardrail/config.yaml

addons/ha-preflight-guardrail/Dockerfile

addons/ha-preflight-guardrail/guardrail.sh

2.4 VS Code Tasks

tools/vscode/tasks.jsonIncludes:

YAML syntax check

Guardrail validation

Combined guardrail suite

2.5 XPipe Command Pack

tools/xpipe/guardrail-pack.jsonIncludes:

validate

repair

guardrail (validate + repair)

2.6 Git Pre‑Commit Hook

tools/hooks/pre-commitEnforces YAML validity before commit.

2.7 Ansible Role

ansible/roles/ha_guardrail/tasks/main.yml

ansible/roles/ha_guardrail/defaults/main.yml

2.8 Documentation

docs/ha-copilot/guardrails.md

docs/ha-copilot/troubleshooting.md

docs/diagrams/guardrail-flow.mmd

🧭 3. Required Mermaid Diagrams

3.1 Guardrail Flow Diagram

The agent must generate:

flowchart TD

    A[Home Assistant Startup] --> B{automations.yaml exists?}
    B -- No --> C[Create automations.yaml with []]
    B -- Yes --> D{YAML parses as list?}

    D -- No --> C
    D -- Yes --> E[Proceed]

    C --> F[Write [] to automations.yaml]
    F --> G[Reload Automations]

    E --> H[ha-copilot Add-on Startup]
    H --> I{get_auto_script_list() returns list?}

    I -- No --> C
    I -- Yes --> J[Add-on Fully Operational]

    subgraph Developer Workflow
        K[VS Code Task: YAML Validation]
        L[Git Pre-Commit Hook]
        M[XPipe Guardrail Command]
    end

    K --> B
    L --> B
    M --> B

3.2 HA ↔ Add-on ↔ Filesystem Sequence Diagram

sequenceDiagram
    participant HA as Home Assistant Core
    participant FS as Filesystem (/config)
    participant GA as Guardrail System
    participant HC as ha-copilot Add-on

    GA->>FS: Validate automations.yaml\n(create or repair if needed)
    FS-->>GA: automations.yaml is valid

    HA->>FS: Load automations.yaml
    FS-->>HA: YAML list returned

    HA->>HC: Start add-on
    HC->>FS: Read automations.yaml via ha_auto_cfg
    FS-->>HC: YAML list returned

    HC->>HA: Add-on ready (WSGI app loaded)

🧬 4. Required Behavior of the Agent

The agent must:

Scaffold all folders exactly as specified

Generate all files with complete content

Ensure all scripts are executable where appropriate

Ensure YAML is valid and lint‑clean

Ensure JSON is valid

Ensure Mermaid diagrams are syntactically correct

Ensure the entire system is self‑healing and reproducible

🧱 5. Output Format

The agent must output:

A complete file tree

Each file with a fenced code block

No placeholders

No TODOs

Fully functional code

🧨 6. Invariant

Every component must enforce:

automations.yaml must always contain a YAML list ([]).